My mother smiles on the screen.
Then she tells me about that morning.
"Do you remember, in January?" she asks.
"Diego bought much too much chocolate for the flight."
I laugh and nod.
I ate the chocolate for weeks.
My mother quietly continues talking.
"Sofia took a photo of all of us at the café."
"We looked at this photo again yesterday."
"Afterwards we waited by the big window for a long time."
"We watched the planes."
"And on the way home Diego said nothing at all."
So my big brother missed me after all.
I look at my mother.
We have not talked about that morning for months.
I hold my phone tightly in my hand.
It is already late in the evening.
But I am not tired at all.
I feel very close to my family right now.
